==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*8 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*15 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Great Ape Luza]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns.
**3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 150 seconds<sup>4,500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Generally much more difficult than the previous two stages, as Pterowl Hazuku shows up and teams up with Luza very early, while Luza covers Hazuku's blind spot entirely, and Li'l Doge dodging can slow you down. To top this off, Wild Doge and Li'l Doge will respawn indefinitely.

Due to the sheer frequent nuking power of Pterowl Hazuku and Great Ape Luza, pretty much all of your attackers should be completely disposable, as most non-spammable Units will simply be a waste of cash.

Breakerblast Cannon is the best Cat Cannon option for this stage, as it can be used to regain ground and even push Luza back and make Pterowl Hazuku vulnerable, as once Hazuku is dead you've basically won the stage.

It's basically required to always to stall at the beginning until you've maxed out your [[Worker Cat]] and filled up your Wallet a good amount before you hit the base. You don't want to try and stall to exhaust all the Owlbrows & Relic Doges as Owlbrow can be much-needed Cash during the fight against Luza and Pterowl Hazuku and the Relic Doges can be extremely valuable stepping stones for Units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] - Greatly helps to stall, as it can get into Hazuku's blind spot and tank several devastating hits from Great Ape Luza.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - Insanely valuable here, but only if timed correctly. Sending them out right after Luza attacks can make sure they don't gain too much ground, and with some Research Combos like BioBone, they can be sent out twice per Luza attack cycle, also making sure Pterowl doesn't create a massive gap in your meatshields if nothing was in their blindspot when they attacked.
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - Retains their incredible value as a meatshield, and can be all the meatshields you need if combined with Boulder Cat and at least 2 Research Up (Sm) CatCombos.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A fantastic spammable attacker capable of dealing great DPS and Damage to all Behemoth Enemies in this stage, being able to deal especially powerful burst damage to Great Ape Luza if stacked on a Relic Doge before the boss wave. They're also great for clearing out peons such as Wild Doge, keeping them from forcing you out of Hazuku's blindspot for a bit. Do note that they work best with some Research Up CatCombos.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Provides great, cheap, and speedy burst damage on both Luza and Hazuku, being able to deal 100,000 Damage to Hazuku at level 50(+3) as well as having the speed to race into their blindspot. They can also help to kill the Owlbrows both when stalling and when actually fighting the boss, However timing is required as they may not accomplish much if spammed blindly, so try and time them whenever there's an opening on Luza & Hazuku.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Another incredible disposable attacker and is great at gathering Cash in the beginning. Money Up & Move Speed Up Talents are required but at this point you should already have both of those Talents maxed.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - Insanely good in this stage, but does require timing to make sure they land a hit. If they can use a Relic Doge or Wild Doge as a stepping stone, they can deal incredible chip damage to Pterowl, as well as weakening any incoming peons making fending them off much easier.
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] - A great pick for this stage in spite of his high cost. Since all of the threatening enemies here are either Behemoth, Floating, or both, his combination of Behemoth Slayer and Strong against Floating works wonders for defense. Plus, Radical Cat is exceptionally strong against Hazuku, as he has '''258,750''' health against him at level 50, on top of not taking chip damage from a rare Surge. If choosing to bring him, it's recommended to level him up to at least 43, as it allows him to survive two hits from Luza instead of just one.
*[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Eraser Cat]] - Can be used similarly to their Manic counterpart, with some major differences; most notably being able to tank hits from Wild Doge, buying invaluable time for attackers to take down one of the fiercest peons in the stage, especially at level 41 or higher, where it can tank 2 hits from him before dying. However, note that it is far more vulnerable from Relic Doge's attacks.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] - Does incredibly well here, as their disposable nature makes them perfect for this stage's required strategy. Their Freeze can lock Luza in place for 6.67s, even longer if their Surge lands on Luza, letting you wail on both Luza and Hazuku freely for a short period. If you get Doron's True Form, their Knockback can expose Pterowl Hazuku, letting you get in a bunch of damage on them to try and take them out of the fight.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Although not as spammable as you'd want, helps a lot here as she can weaken Luza and prevent him from killing your attackers in Hazuku's blindspot as fast. Furthermore, if one's strategy is to nuke Luza as much as possible before Hazuku shows up, then Naala would be required to make sure that your attackers dont die to Luza instantly and are able to deliver the damage that would cripple or outright kill Luza.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] - The key to the strategy of nuking Luza before Hazuku shows up, with the help of Doron, Awakened Naala and Thunderbolt Cannon (or alternatively, something to Knockback/flinch and interrupt Luza should it try to retaliate, which can also buy time). By shutting down Luza this way, it will become much easier to deal with the rest.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - Does extremely well here due to his massive waves that freeze Pterowl Hazuku as well as clear up any peons that are on the stage. Cosmo has a standing range of 850, so as long as you are able to knock back Pterowl Hazuku once or use Great Ape Luza as a stepping stone, this stage can be cleared with minimal difficulty. This is due to Luza having a Omni-strike range of 700, while Pterowl has a LD range of 1060.
*[[Talents|Talented and Ultra Talented]] [[Sodom (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Sodom]] - Also does fantastically here with his [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Floating and Relic, and combined with his [[Behemoth Slayer]] Ultra Talent, Sodom is able to eat hits from Hazuku and Luza like they were tasty rocks and dirt. He's an earth dragon, what else would he eat? Do be wary of the Wild Doges though, as they will rip and tear through Sodom's HP in a matter of seconds.

==Trivia==
*The enemy base is similar to that of the [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] stage.
*This stage reuses music from the [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku Invasion]].
*This is one of the only stages in the game that has a chance of rewarding a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], the others being [[Villains Jungle]], [[Unkept Promises]], [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Aku Altar's Seal]], [[Reign of the Ape Lord]] and [[Ape Lord's Revenge]].

